// 5 real damage-dealing affinities (Neutral = no element). Fire/Ice/Rock keep their own baseline
// status on landing (Burn/Slow/Intimidate); Void and Lightning have none - their identity is
// hand-authored WeaponDataAsset traits instead (e.g. a Lightning gun starting with Ricochet, a Void
// gun starting with Pierce - Void's own flavor is inward displacement/negative knockback, not a
// status). Landing any of the 5 on a target already carrying a Rift Mark (see
// StatusEffects.RiftMarkStacks) consumes one stack and fires that element's own reaction -
// Fire->Detonation, Ice->Deep Freeze, Rock->Rupture, Lightning->Overload, Void->Singularity - see
// docs/elemental-reactions.md. Lightning appended at the end (not inserted alongside Rock/Void) to
// avoid renumbering Void's existing ordinal in already-serialized assets.
enum ElementType : Byte
{
    Neutral,
    Fire,
    Ice,
    Rock,
    Void,
    Lightning
}
